Z||000000||85fierogt||08-05-2001||10:49 PM||||aight guys im new to this whole fiero game i just bought a 85 gt 2.8 litre v6 4 speed and i got some questions first of all what is the factory ride height from like the ground to the bottom of the car, second where can i find white face guages for the 85 that go past 80 mph, how is the fiero store, legit? and ill post more as the come to me oh and the kid i bought it for said he put a chip in, hwo do i verify this, thanxs<BR>-brad AKA 85fierogt<p>[This message has been edited by 85fierogt (edited 08-05-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||Oreif||08-05-2001||11:08 PM||||The ride height from factory is 6" from frame to ground. The Fiero Store is very legit. I've ordered many items from them. They have very good customer service. If you join/belong to a Fiero club, They will take 10% off of everything except the genuine GM parts they stock. (Usually the electrical switches and seals) As for white Gauges, I am not familiar with what is available or where.<BR>To verify the chip, Just remove the cover from the ECM (Electronic Control Module) It is located under the center console mounted to the rear firewall. (Under the glove box).<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||08-05-2001||11:12 PM||||I believe there are some speedometers on the mall section. Several members also sell them & check out parts vendors at top of page. The Fiero Store has been around a long time, I've personally never had a problem with them. I've heard their web site is down right now.||||reg||1
